            <ArticleTitle>[Hyperuricemia: explain, ignore or treat?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>797-801</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Human purin metabolism is summarized briefly and the terms primary and secondary gout are defined. Asymptomatic hyperuricemia as a risk factor for gout, urate nephropathy and ischemic heart disease is discussed. Treatment modalities of hyperuricemia are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
